content.text:
Now CSS menu scrim and mobile adjustments. Add to `.menu-inner` an isolation and ::before; child z-index. Also maybe dim title brightness a bit. Let's add:

```
.menu-inner { isolation: isolate; }
.menu-inner::before {
  content:''; position:absolute; inset:-6% -10%; z-index:-1;
  background: radial-gradient(ellipse at 50% 46%, rgba(2,7,14,.66) 0%, rgba(2,7,14,.42) 45%, rgba(2,7,14,0) 72%);
  filter: blur(10px);
  pointer-events:none;
}
```
z-index -1 within isolated stacking context = behind content but above menu background? In an isolated stacking context, negative z-index child renders behind the element's own background but still within context; menu-inner has no background, so it shows above parent's background. Good.

But the scrim only covers menu-inner size (880x?), and the title is large, may extend beyond? h1 130px, menu-inner width 880, title "1V1 ARENA" fits. Fine.

Mobile menu-inner width 92vw, scrim covers. Good.

Title gradient: top white; over dark scrim will be great.

For mobile, the menu title vertical is fine. Subtitle and banner overlap will be hidden by scrim.

Also maybe add `padding` so the scrim doesn't clip. inset -6% -10%.

Apply.

